<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rao Siha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1273</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Rao Sheoji</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rao Siha was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore dynasty</a> of Marwar, who according to tradition came from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> region and settled near Pali in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> in the 13th century. A memorial stone at Bithu records his death in 1273. His descendants built the Rathore states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a>, Bikaner and others.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rao-siha.jpg" alt="Rao Siha" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PD · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Jodhpur.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
